d 'XLIMAGE': module to insert or replace an image in an Excel workbook without stacking copies and without Python
d
d     xlimage places an image in an Excel workbook at the specified
d cell. If that cell does not yet hold an image, the image is	
d inserted; if one is already anchored there, it is replaced. In
d both cases it avoids the common problem with putexcel, whereby   
d re-running a do-file does not overwrite images but stacks new
d copies at the same position, inflating the file with invisible   
d duplicates.	 Because of this, the same command line can be used
d on every run: the first time it inserts and later runs replace,
d with no    duplicated code and no stacked images. The title,
d tables, formatting, and other images in the workbook are left
d untouched. 
d
d KW: image handling
d KW: Excel
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260820
d
d Author: Mario Anderson Apaza Ñaupa,  NA
d Support: email marioapaza@@outlook.com
d
f xlimage.ado
